p comedians like  chris rock  dave chappelle bill burr and so on and  so forth  so as soon as i found out stand-up  comedians had their own podcast shows  i was instantly hooked on phonics and  this is when i found the joe rogan  experience  i've been a fan since brian redband was  on the show and they would film episodes  out of the back of the ice house  finding this show back then was exactly  what i needed in my life  it almost instantly became one of my  favorite things to listen to  in fact i would say it even influenced  me into making videos of my own  even now i would say i listen to more  podcasts than i do music  which is kinda crazy to think about  there was really nothing else like it  out there that you could find for free  now i know one of joe rogan's biggest  influences was the opie and anthony show  but that was not a show that was offered  for free neither was howard stern for  that matter  those shows were on siriusxm and even  some of the other great podcasters did  not have a show quite like joe's  marc maron and adam corolla had big  shows at the time but they were still  doing your interview style shows  the joe rogan experience was very  different it felt very natural  as if you were hanging out with your own  friends one of the main reasons it felt  like  this is because joe would have all of  his best friends on the show  he never brought them on to interview  them either they would all just talk  about whatever they wanted  whenever i would watch or listen to one  of his new episodes i felt like i was a  fly on the wall  it felt like i was listening to my own  friends have a conversation  this is what made the show so great for  me now i will admit i don't listen to  every single episode that is released  but i do see most of them  if you're a big fan like i am then you  will know joe has a handful of friends  that are on his show  nearly once a month if he does one of  his fight companions then he might have  some of his friends on several times  that month  it just depends on how things work out  and this is what led to me becoming a  fan of some of his other friends who are  stand-up comedians like bert kreischer  tom segura joey diaz brian callan  theo vaughn and so many others my  favorite episodes are when joe has on  the og's from back in the day  like his best friends so as soon as  everyone started to realize how  successful joe's show was becoming  they all started shows of their own joey  diaz started the church of what's  happening now  with his sidekick lee syed then brian  callan started the fighter and the kid  with the former ufc fighter brendan  schaub theo  vaughn also has his own show this past  weekend  because of the joe rogan experience i  became a fan of all these other  comedians  and their own respective shows one of  the things i loved about this group of  friends is how they built this community  with one another  but this is all about the change the  stand-up comedy and podcasting scene in  los angeles california will never be the  same  now i will say there are a lot of things  that do factor into all of these changes  before i go any further and speculate on  anything i do want to make sure everyone  keeps this in mind  i am simply an outsider looking in  obviously i don't know any of these guys  in real life  i'm only a fan who wants to give his  opinion on what's happening lately  now if you're watching this video then i  assume you already know joe rogan is  moving out of los angeles  he has already had a new studio made in  texas where he will be living for the  foreseeable future  i was actually watching joe's show right  before i sat down to make the video and  in his most recent episode he sat down  with his friend duncan  and according to joe he says he does not  think giant cities like los angeles are  sustainable  when the city is running great then  things are wonderful  before covent 19 the comedy store was  sold out almost every night  the restaurants were 